      "question": {
        ":question/id": "e46c1f08-e3d6-51c4-a8f5-c9afcf2c9c4e",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "If $f(x)=\\frac{\\sin x}{{x}^{2}},$ find ${f}^{\\prime}(x).$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\sin x$ and $v(x)={x}^{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\\prime}(x)&=\\frac{u^{\\prime}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot v^{\\prime}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})^{\\prime}\\cdot (x^{2})-(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (x^{2})^{\\prime}}{(x^{2})^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{{x}^{2}\\cos x-2xsinx}{{x}^{4}}\\\\ &=\\frac{x(xcosx-2\\sin x)}{{x}^{4}}\\\\ &=\\frac{xcosx-2\\sin x}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
